Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='signatures', at=datetime(2026, 10, 6, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title="Signatures are the deployment's, from [signatures] root; every writer signs and the door checks the proof", body="*Signatures are the deployment's, from `[signatures] root`* (2026-10-06, SPEC law 42; `suzatary_core::signatures`), which every instance declares (`suzatary init` writes it; there is no unsigned path). Every writer signs: the tab with its device key, the box with the root (`SUZATARY_BOX_KEY`), the agent's replica with its own, and each actor is registered with the key its writes are signed by and no other (`signatures::Custody`: the agent's for `triage` whatever `untrusted` names; `device init` repairs a box where it was not); the trusted keys are `KeyAdded`/`KeyRevoked` objects the root signed (by a tapped device card, by `suzatary device trust`, or by a one-time code `suzatary device pair` prints, which trusts the key that signs the request carrying it: ten minutes, one use, five tries, kept only as a keyed hash and never logged; `signatures::Pairing`), and `POST /api/objects` refuses a write no trusted key of its actor proves, beside the `act_as` gate; every other write route asks the same of the request (`Trust::admits`, the one door), performs it once, pushes its provenance in `requests/` (who asked, what it wrote; never a body or an answer, which stays on the box for a replay), and the server and `device init` adopt each chain (resolving the keys only reads). The readings still fold under `Untrusted`, not `Proven`: history beneath each chain's epoch is unsigned and stays valid, so the proof is enforced at the door and shown, never a second policy. A request a revoked key signs, a read included (the tab signs its reads), is answered with the wipe (`410`), and the tab deletes what it holds; a key is revoked at the terminal alone (`suzatary device revoke`, 2026-10-09). A wipe clears the device's copy and stops nothing else: reads stay open to any device on the owner's Tailscale login, so removing the device from the tailnet is the real cut-off.", rationale='Decided 2026-10-06 (SPEC law 42); a key is revoked at the terminal alone since 2026-10-09.', supersedes=()))